```java
@Modifying
@Query("UPDATE Post p SET p.viewCount = p.viewCount + 1 WHERE p.id = :id")
void incrementViewCount(@Param("id") Long id);
```
`@Modifying` has **no** `clearAutomatically = true`.

**PostLikeRepository.java (line 17):**
```java
@Modifying(clearAutomatically = true, flushAutomatically = true)
```
`@Modifying` **does** have `clearAutomatically = true` (and `flushAutomatically = true`).

**PostService.java getPostById (lines 91-103):**
```java
@Transactional
public PostResponse getPostById(Long id) {
    postRepository.incrementViewCount(id);
    Post post = postRepository.findById(id)
            .orElseThrow(() -> new ResourceNotFoundException("帖子不存在"));
    ...
}
```
The call order is confirmed: `incrementViewCount(id)` is called first, then `findById(id)`, all within a single `@Transactional` method.

---

**CONFIRMED** -- `PostRepository.incrementViewCount` uses bare `@Modifying` without `clearAutomatically=true`, so the JPA persistence context is not cleared after the bulk UPDATE, causing the subsequent `findById` in the same `@Transactional` method to return the stale cached entity with the old `viewCount` rather than fetching the incremented value from the database.

